        "#REGLA COMPESTA DE SIMPSON"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "z3OhMI0-wiNd"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Omwk8pAZqLvL"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import sympy as sy\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Para la Regla Compuesta de Simpson tenemos la fórmula\n",
        "  $\\int_{a}^{b} f(x)dx \\ = \\frac {h}{3}[f(a) + 2 \\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{n}{2} - 1} f(x_{2j}) + 4 \\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} f(x_{2j-1}) + f(b)] - \\frac{b-a}{180}h^4f^{IV}(M) $"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f_BR1F8CxMXc"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Definimos la función a calcular"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eKyYxdJBfhHE"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def f(x):\n",
        "  return np.exp(2*x)* np.sin(3*x) #definimos la funcion"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SkrTepg2tuwI"
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Ahora definimos quienes son \"n\" y \"h\" para la regla compuesta de Simpson y con la restricción que \"n\" es entero y par, $h= \\frac{b-a}{n}$"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DwAnepRoiWET"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "b=0\n",
        "a=2\n",
        "n=54\n",
        "h= (b-a)/n\n",
        "XI0 = f(a) + f(b) #la suma de estos dos terminos son lo que estan dentro del corchete\n",
        "XI1 = 0 #XI1 y XI2 son acomuladores para los terminos con sumatorias\n",
        "XI2 = 0"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Th-quW9jiq12"
      },
      "execution_count": 32,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Notemos que con los subíndices en las sumatorias $f(x_{2j})$ es par y $f(x_{2j-1})$ son impares para $i = 1,2,...,n-1$"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "htl0wZTCtwQu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "for i in range(1,n):\n",
        " X = a + i*h\n",
        "if i % 2 == 0:\n",
        "  XI2 = XI2 + f(X)\n",
        "else :\n",
        "    XI1 = XI1 + f(X)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "G3sABQgQn52A"
      },
      "execution_count": 37,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        " XI = (h/3)*(XI0 + 2*XI2 + 4*XI1)\n",
        " print(f\"{XI}\")"
      ],
